\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\f0\fs22\lang9 Disk Collection Browser \b0 - enhanced user interface for RespeQt Atari floppy disk drive emulation\par
 \b Concept:\b0  The Disk Collection Browser (aka Disk Browser), allows the user to conveniently load and unload floppy disk image files with the click of the mouse from one simple dialog box. This creates a nostalgic approximation of the floppy disk flip files where an Atari user would commonly keep their collection of disks.\par
As a first-time user of RespeQt, I was confused by the main screen with its array of 15 virtual drives (1 - 9 and J - O).  Why would anyone who used the Atari computer in its time have owned more than 1 or 2 floppy drives? ... Apparently, the usefulness of this array becomes more apparent as one tries to paruse their collection of ATR backup files to find a program of interest to load and run on the Atari.  Once you find your favorites, it's somewhat less painful to mount them all on the virtual drives and swap the target disk to drive 1 for booting.\par
As an old-school Atari user and software developer, I was devoted to creating the user experience that represented how it felt to sit in front of the computer and interact with the software as it was 40 years ago.  This is my contribution to the project:\par

