Note, fonts are customizable including color, bold, italics and 'B' side layout as shown above.\par
\b Store DB settings with App settings\b0  - (the default option) stores the full path names of your collections in the OS standard settings location. On Windows, this will be in the system registry, underneath the key for Software/ZeeSoft/RespeQt/DiskBrowserDlg/Artwork. Under each collection will be full path names of disks with pics or custom label text.\par
\b Subdir .respeqt_db in each folder\b0  - looks for, or creates, a sub-directory named ".respeqt_db" in each collection folder in which you have set custom pics or labels. The advantage of this option is the entire folder can be moved without having to reassign new path names/locations of custom artwork. An individual JSON file (one per folder/collection) is used to store assigned files and text.\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b Store DB settings in AppData folder\b0  - similar to the App settings option, however this creates a JSON file in the specific or custom folder. On windows, this will default to the current user's "AppData" folder which is typically hidden under C:\\Users\\username\\AppData. The advantage of this option is that it creates a file that can be easily edited/maintained with a text editor.\par
\b Copy pics to\b0  <\i target\i0 > - where \i target\i0  depends on the source option selected above. A file is copied to the designated \i target\i0  when the user invokes the preview pic context menu and selects a picture elsewhere in the host file system.\par
\b Scan and Parse filenames for pics/labels\b0  -in addition to the above 3 main sources for pics and labels, the program will search the file system for specific named files for preview pics and label text. This scheme is enumerated as follows:\line 1. Basename with viable image extension.\line     ex: DiskBaseName.png or *.jpg, etc... any Qt supported format can be used.\line 2. Matching index prefixed image file in the disk folder. Note index B designates the reverse side of a floppy disk.\line     ex: disk name = 12b.Title of Disk.ATR ("Title of Disk" appears on the label if no PNG present)\line            image file = 12b.Menu Screen.PNG (screen shot of a disk that boots to a game menu)\line     or: image file = 12b.PNG\line 3. Use the hard-coded/generic name respeqt_db.* for default thumbnail.\line     ex: respeqt_db.png \par
\b Favor AppData/JSON over filename scheme\b0  - with this option selected, the user can override the results of the file name scan described above. This is intuitive because the action of choosing a specific pic or clicking the label and typing in a disk title should normally show by default. Disabling this option may result in unexpected behavior but is available for testing and troubleshooting.\par
\b Floppy Labels\b0  -these fields control the font selection and attributes for the label title text and index label areas on the generic floppy disk pictures. Face name, bold, italic, color and scale factors are customizable. Note the label title and index only appear over the built-in floppy disk images.\par
